{"step_index":62,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:09:08Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Walkthrough of the SnapDialer mobile application implementation, including database schema, power dialer HUD, vision extraction, cadence engine, and iPhone testing guide.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Walkthrough: \"Snap-to-Dial\" Mobile Power Dialer (iOS & Android)\n\nWe have created the full codebase for **SnapDialer** at [`C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer).\n\nThe app is built with **React Native (Expo)**, **SQLite (`expo-sqlite`)**, and an **On-Device Vision & Multimodal Extraction Pipeline**, providing a **\\$0.00 backend hosting cost** model.\n\n---\n\n## What Has Been Built\n\n### 1. Local SQLite Storage Engine ([`src/db/`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db))\n- **`database.ts`:** Creates SQLite tables with WAL mode, foreign keys, and indexes:\n  - `lists`: Stores digitized lead sheets, completion %, and connect counts.\n  - `leads`: Stores individual contacts, phone numbers, attempt counts, notes, and cadence steps.\n  - `call_logs`: Logs timestamps, call durations, dispositions, and sent SMS records.\n  - `cadence_rules` & `sms_templates`: Configurable automated follow-up sequences.\n- **`leadsRepository.ts`:** Batch-inserts extracted leads from photos, updates 1-tap dispositions, and dynamically filters the active dialing queue.\n- **`callLogsRepository.ts`:** Computes analytics summaries (total dials, connect rates, bad number counts).\n\n### 2. Document Capture & Vision AI Parser ([`src/services/visionService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/visionService.ts))\n- Captures or imports photos of paper lead sheets, sign-in forms, or handwritten rosters.\n- Formats image for structured JSON extraction via **Gemini 2.5 Flash Vision** (free tier) or local demo parsing.\n- Automatically cleans and sanitizes phone numbers into dialable formats.\n\n### 3. Power Dialer HUD ([`src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx))\n- **Active Queue Manager:** Displays the current contact's name, phone, company, notes, and attempt badge (`Attempt #2`).\n- **One-Tap Calling:** Direct trigger via native cellular bridge (`tel://`).\n- **Oversized 1-Tap Disposition Controls:**\n  - 🚫 **No Answer / VM Drop:** Logs attempt, checks cadence rules, auto-advances.\n  - ⚡ **Bad Number:** Disqualifies contact, removes from queue.\n  - 💬 **Quick Text:** Opens native SMS with personalized template (`{{name}}`).\n  - 🤝 **Connected:** Opens quick-note modal to record deal notes.\n- **Pacing Engine:** 3-second auto-advance countdown banner with pause control.\n\n### 4. Cadence & SMS Automation Engine ([`src/services/cadenceEngine.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/cadenceEngine.ts))\n- Evaluates rules on every call attempt (e.g. *If Attempt = 2 AND Outcome = No Answer $\\rightarrow$ Prompt Follow-up SMS #1*).\n- Dynamic token interpolation replaces `{{name}}` and `{{company}}` automatically.\n\n### 5. Analytics & JSON/CSV Data Export ([`src/screens/AnalyticsScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/AnalyticsScreen.tsx))\n- Real-time connect rate percentage, dials breakdown, and share sheet export.\n\n---\n\n## How to Test Live on Your iPhone\n\n1. Open your terminal in the project directory:\n   ```bash\n   cd C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\n   ```\n2. Install dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n3. Start the Expo development server:\n   ```bash\n   npx expo start\n   ```\n4. Open the **Camera app** on your iPhone and scan the **QR code** displayed on your screen.\n5. Tap **Open in Expo Go**. The app will compile and launch on your iPhone.\n","Description":"Walkthrough artifact documenting completed SnapDialer implementation and iPhone testing instructions","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Writing walkthrough artifact","toolSummary":"Write walkthrough.md"}}]}
