{"step_index":64,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:09:14Z","content":"The complete implementation of **SnapDialer** has been scaffolded and written to:\n\n📂 **[`C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer)**\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Recommended Workspace:** You can set `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer` as your active workspace directory in Antigravity.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Local SQLite Architecture (\\$0 Backend Hosting Cost):**\n   - Implemented in [`src/db/database.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/database.ts), [`src/db/leadsRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/leadsRepository.ts), [`src/db/callLogsRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/callLogsRepository.ts), and [`src/db/cadenceRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/cadenceRepository.ts).\n   - Keeps all lead sheets, call records, dispositions, and cadence states offline-first in the phone's sandboxed local SQLite database.\n2. **AI Lead Sheet Ingestion:**\n   - [`src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx) & [`src/services/visionService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/visionService.ts).\n   - Allows snapping a photo of any physical lead sheet, parsing names/numbers into a clean, editable data table before importing to SQLite.\n3. **Power Dialer HUD:**\n   - [`src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx).\n   - Large 1-tap outcome buttons: 🚫 **No Answer / VM**, ⚡ **Bad Number**, 💬 **Quick Text**, and 🤝 **Connected** (with quick-notes scratchpad), plus a 3-second auto-advance countdown timer.\n4. **Cadence Engine & Native SIM Bridge:**\n   - [`src/services/cadenceEngine.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/cadenceEngine.ts) & [`src/services/telephonyService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/telephonyService.ts).\n   - Multi-touch sequencing (e.g. *Attempt 2 $\\rightarrow$ Auto-prompt follow-up SMS if unanswered*) using your phone's unlimited cellular plan (`tel:` and `sms:` URI schemes).\n5. **Analytics & Data Export:**\n   - [`src/screens/AnalyticsScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/AnalyticsScreen.tsx).\n\n---\n\n### How to Run & Test on Your iPhone:\n\n1. In your terminal, navigate to the project directory:\n   ```bash\n   cd C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\n   ```\n2. Install dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n3. Start the development server:\n   ```bash\n   npx expo start\n   ```\n4. Open the **Camera app** on your iPhone, scan the **QR code** in your terminal, and tap **Open in Expo Go**.\n\nFor complete details, check the **[Walkthrough Document](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/walkthrough.md)**."}
