{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:31:54Z","content":"The error occurred because **Expo SDK 52** requires `expo-asset` and `expo-font` for its internal Metro bundler pipeline.\n\nI have updated your [`package.json`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/package.json) and cleaned the [`app.json`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/app.json) configuration.\n\n---\n\n### To fix this and display the QR code:\n\nRun this command in your terminal inside `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer`:\n\n```bash\nnpm install expo-asset expo-font expo-constants\n```\n\nThen start Expo:\n\n```bash\nnpx expo start\n```\n\n---\n\n### What to expect:\n1. The terminal will display the **interactive QR Code**.\n2. Open the **Camera app** on your iPhone.\n3. Point your camera at the QR code and tap **Open in Expo Go**.\n4. The SnapDialer app will load immediately on your iPhone.\n\n*(Tip: If your iPhone and computer are on different Wi-Fi networks or a VPN, run `npx expo start --tunnel` instead).*"}
{"step_index":78,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:35:35Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nI followed your instructions and got:\n\nC:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer>npx expo start --tunnel\r\nStarting project at C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\r\nStarting Metro Bundler\r\n√ The package @expo/ngrok@^4.1.0 is required to use tunnels, would you like to install it globally? ... yes\r\nInstalling @expo/ngrok@^4.1.0...\r\n> npm install --global @expo/ngrok@^4.1.0\r\nInstalled @expo/ngrok@^4.1.0\r\nCommandError: failed to start tunnel\r\n\r\nremote gone away\r\n\r\nCheck the Ngrok status page for outages: https://status.ngrok.com/\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-18T09:35:35-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":79,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:35:35Z","content":"The `--tunnel` flag uses a 3rd-party service (ngrok) that can be blocked by Windows Firewall or experience temporary service drops.\n\nYou don't need `--tunnel` if your iPhone and PC are connected to the same Wi-Fi network.\n\n---\n\n### Solution 1: Run in Standard LAN Mode (Recommended)\n\nMake sure your **iPhone is on the same Wi-Fi** as your PC, then run:\n\n```bash\nnpx expo start -c\n```\n\n*(The `-c` clears the bundler cache to ensure a clean startup).*\n\n1. A large **QR code** will appear directly in your terminal.\n2. If Windows prompts you with a **Windows Defender Firewall** popup asking to allow `Node.js`, click **Allow access** (Private networks).\n3. Open the **Camera app on your iPhone**, scan the QR code, and tap **Open in Expo Go**.\n\n---\n\n### Solution 2: If on Different Networks (Expo Account Sync)\n\nIf your PC and iPhone cannot talk over local Wi-Fi:\n\n1. Create a free account at [expo.dev](https://expo.dev) if you haven't already.\n2. Log into Expo in your terminal:\n   ```bash\n   npx expo login\n   ```\n3. Log into the same account inside the **Expo Go app** on your iPhone.\n4. Run `npx expo start` in your terminal.\n5. In the Expo Go app on your iPhone, the **SnapDialer** project will automatically appear at the top under **\"Recently in development\"**—just tap it to open!"}
