{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T13:40:29Z","content":"Let's get this resolved in 2 quick steps:\n\n### Step 1: Auto-Align the Package Versions\nRun this command in your terminal to automatically align the packages with Expo's recommended versions:\n\n```bash\nnpx expo install --fix\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Why the iPhone is Not Connecting (Common Windows Fix)\n\nWhen an iPhone cannot load `exp://` from a Windows PC, it is almost always due to one of two things:\n\n#### A. Windows Defender Firewall is Blocking Port 8081\n1. On your Windows PC, open **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Network & Internet $\\rightarrow$ Wi-Fi** (or Ethernet).\n2. Click on your active connection and make sure **Network profile type** is set to **Private** (if it is set to \"Public\", Windows blocks all iPhone/LAN connections).\n\n#### B. Check if Expo is using the Right Wi-Fi IP\nIf you have Docker, WSL, or a VPN running, Expo might be printing an internal virtual IP instead of your actual Wi-Fi router IP.\n\n1. Open PowerShell or Command Prompt and run:\n   ```bash\n   ipconfig\n   ```\n2. Look for **IPv4 Address** under your **Wireless LAN adapter Wi-Fi** (usually starts with `192.16